# Line-ending policy.
#
# Store everything as LF in the repository and check out native endings locally.
# This matters because the app is developed on Windows but deployed to Linux:
# without it, files can reach the server with CRLF, and git prints a
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every single add.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Windows launcher is the exception. cmd.exe can mis-parse a batch file that
# uses bare LF endings, particularly around labels and goto, so this one is
# always checked out with CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
